  "label": "The text '49 people were killed at christchurch' is mapped onto the smiling man labeled 'muslim'.",
  "description": "The top panel's text '49 people were killed at christchurch' is juxtaposed with the visual of a smiling man labeled 'muslim'. This mapping implies that the man represents or embodies the reaction (or lack thereof) to the event described in the text, specifically portraying him as indifferent or insensitive to the tragedy. The text explicitly labels the event, and the visual material (the man) is mapped onto this event through the label 'muslim', creating an analogical mapping where the man is presented as a representative of the Muslim community's supposed reaction to the Christchurch shootings.",
